description:
File: rust/lichen-schc/src/fragment.rs
Lines: 873-876

The receiver correctly compares retransmitted fragment content against stored content and aborts if they differ:

  if *bitmap & bit != 0 {
      if destination != fragment.payload {
          return self.abort(fragment.rule_id);
      }

This prevents an attacker from injecting different content via retransmission attacks. Worth defending if anyone suggests removing this check.
